      "id": "https://www.alpinelinux.org/posts/2026-11-05-openssh-password-authentication-bypass/",
      "url": "https://www.alpinelinux.org/posts/2026-11-05-openssh-password-authentication-bypass/",
      "title": "Alpine warns of OpenSSH login bypass in tiny-cloud images",
      "content_html": "Alpine Linux says its official tiny-cloud images from versions 3.18.11 through 3.24.3 can expose users to an OpenSSH login bypass. An attacker who can reach SSH can use an unusually long password to access some passwordless accounts. On these images, the alpine account can then use passwordless doas to gain root access. The images are safe on first boot but become vulnerable once a SHA-512 password hash exists on the machine, such as after an administrator sets a console password or user data adds a user with a hashed password. Images built from patched point releases 3.21.10, 3.22.8, 3.23.8 and 3.24.4 include the fix. Existing instances running earlier versions need an update or must have password authentication disabled.",
      "date_published": "2026-11-07T14:51:26+00:00",
