      "title": "Democratic election gains open new state climate policy battles",
      "content_html": "Democrats’ midterm gains have given the party unified control of state government in Arizona, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, where clean-energy and climate policies have lagged or faced Republican resistance. In Wisconsin, advocates are seeking utility planning requirements and a clean-power standard; Pennsylvania Democrats are considering appliance efficiency rules, community and rooftop solar, and transit funding.\n\nAt the federal level, Rep. Jared Huffman, the incoming House Natural Resources Committee chairman, says Democrats should write their own permitting legislation rather than accept the Senate-negotiated bill, which he argues could weaken protections for endangered species, tribes and clean water. Democrats will control both chambers of Congress beginning in January 2027.",
