      "id": "https://www.businessinsider.com/married-later-life-wanted-separate-bedrooms-changed-mind-2026-11",
      "url": "https://www.businessinsider.com/married-later-life-wanted-separate-bedrooms-changed-mind-2026-11",
      "title": "I told my husband I wanted a sleep divorce before we got married. He thought sleeping apart meant I didn't love him.",
      "content_html": "\"I want separate bedrooms,\" I blurted out, trying to sound casual. \"It's practical, not personal; I'm just such a light sleeper and…\" But Michael was frowning. I knew it bothered him. I didn't know then it was a potential dealbreaker. I met Michael, an Air Force veteran and former fire chief, at our 55+ senior living community, where we bonded over themed dress-up parties. Our first was Gatsby, and we had a blast transforming into full characters while our fellow residents cheered us on. With every costume change, we grew closer and spent nights at each other's apartments. Those sleepovers",
