      "title": "Novartis to halt pelacarsen development for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease after trial finds no benefit",
      "content_html": "Novartis will stop developing pelacarsen to prevent heart attacks and other cardiovascular events after a large trial found the drug did not reduce serious outcomes, despite sharply lowering lipoprotein(a), or Lp(a), a genetically linked blood particle. Results presented Nov. 7 in Chicago showed no meaningful difference in heart attacks, strokes, cardiovascular deaths or urgent artery procedures among 8,350 participants followed for a median of 4.7 years. The company will continue a separate trial in people with aortic valve disease.\n\nHigh Lp(a) affects an estimated one in five people worldwide, and no treatment specifically targets it. A separate Novo Nordisk trial found that its anti-inflammatory drug ziltivekimab did not prevent major heart events, despite reducing inflammation as intended. Other Lp(a) drugs remain in development: Amgen expects Phase 3 results in early 2028, and Eli Lilly expects its results in 2029.",
